# Build artifacts
/bin/
/dist/
/out/
*.exe
*.test
*.out

# Python bytecode. The AI runtime targets 3.11+ and the standard library only,
# so a committed .pyc is a build artifact that pins an interpreter nobody else
# runs, and it gets stale silently.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# Test and coverage output. `go test -coverprofile=coverage` writes a plain
# file at the repo root, which is easy to stage by accident.
/coverage
/coverage.*

# Local runtime state — never commit evidence, logs, secrets or checkpoints
/data/
/evidence/
/logs/
/secrets/
/checkpoints/
*.key
*.pem

# Replay fixtures captured from a live system may contain real site data.
# Sanitized, reviewed fixtures only. The sanitiser is the single choke point
# between a live source and a committed file: internal/fixture/sanitize.go.
# See internal/README.md.
/fixtures/private/
/testdata/private/

# Tooling
/tools/bin/
/.protoc/
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Editors
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
.DS_Store
